# Citation File Format — CrashX

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CrashX: Fine-Tuning and Evaluating Video Language Models for Traffic Accident Explanation"
message: "If you use this software, evaluation protocol, or paper draft, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dharpure
    given-names: Harshal
repository-code: "https://github.com/harshalDharpure/Crash-X"
url: "https://github.com/harshalDharpure/Crash-X"
abstract: >-
  CrashX studies whether Video-LLMs can faithfully explain dashcam traffic
  accidents on the Car Crash Dataset. Domain adaptation (CrashLogic-7B) reduces
  omissions and improves lexical metrics but does not reduce hallucinations;
  temporal localisation behaves like a dataset prior; mild temporal contrastive
  decoding is not significant under paired tests.
keywords:
  - video-llm
  - traffic accident
  - hallucination
  - omission
  - faithfulness
  - temporal grounding
  - QLoRA
  - contrastive decoding
  - Car Crash Dataset
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
